From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valentin rameau <valentin.rameau@outlook.fr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:04:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/33] Trace $4200-$421F writes on the Vita host

The $2100-$213F probe added with the Vita host covers the display registers,
but the raster split chain is armed through $4200 (NMI/IRQ enable) and
$4207-$420A (H/V timer targets). Without those a host cannot tell an unarmed
chain from a chain that armed and was never serviced.

Vita-only, inside the existing #ifdef VITA probe pattern.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runner/src/common_rtl.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runner/src/common_rtl.c b/runner/src/common_rtl.c
index bbd9599..d2ce982 100644
--- a/runner/src/common_rtl.c
+++ b/runner/src/common_rtl.c
@@ -1420,6 +1420,13 @@ void WriteReg(uint16 reg, uint8 value) {
   } else if (reg >= 0x2180 && reg < 0x2184) {
     snes_writeBBus(g_snes, reg & 0xff, value);
   } else if (reg >= 0x4200 && reg < 0x4220) {
+#ifdef VITA
+    /* Vita bring-up probe: the raster split chain is armed through $4200
+     * (NMI/IRQ enable) and $4207-$420A (H/V timer targets). Trace those to
+     * see whether the chain is armed at all, and at which line. */
+    { extern void FZeroLogCpuRegWrite(uint16 reg, uint8 value, int line);
+      FZeroLogCpuRegWrite(reg, value, g_snes ? (int)g_snes->vPos : -1); }
+#endif
     if (reg == 0x420C) {
       g_snesrecomp_last_hdmaen = value;
       /* Per-line fact: this title switches the transition's HDMA
